PATCH 499: the MGA DAC-capture entry 0660 spun forever -- the AZER1 self-play hang.

FUN_0000_0660 (asm 0x660-0x730) is FUN_0000_04f1's exact twin and carried the identical defect patch 092
fixed there:
    6be: bb 88 07        mov  bx,0x788
    6c1: 8c d9           mov  cx,ds
    6c3: b8 00 03        mov  ax,0x300
    6c6: ff 1e e4 00     lcall [DGROUP:0xe4]      ; the device-object palette method
    6ca: 72 35           jb   0x701               ; CF selects CLEAR (1) vs CAPTURE (0)
Ghidra dropped BOTH the method's three register arguments (it emitted `(...)(0)`) and its returned CF,
inventing `bVar6 = false` and folding the whole CF==0 branch into `if (!bVar6) { do { } while (true); }`.

Until patch 497 repaired the CS=0 weapon-station dispatch nothing ever fired, so the impact cascade never
ran and this was unreachable.  With 497 an AZER1 self-play HANGS between t=6500 and t=6800, stack:
  0660 <- 0647 <- 063c <- a5c4 <- a93e <- b39c <- c336 <- c31e <- bbb7 <- b5e7
i.e. the first projectile impact resolved against the player.  (My crash sweep scored the hang as
"ran clean" because a hung run and a survived run both end in the timeout; the sweep now needs a
progress check, not just an exit code.)

Reconstructed 1:1 from the asm:
  CF==0 (0x6cc-0x700): wait one INT-8 tick on DGROUP:0x44e -- `mov ax,[0x44e]; L: cmp [0x44e],ax; je L`,
        driven by the cooperative fist_timer_pump(), the same idiom as 04f1's fade path and patch 017 --
        then incb [0x738], read the whole 768-byte DAC through ports 0x3c7/0x3c9 into the buffer SEGMENT
        word[0x788], decb [0x738], and arm the 0x732 continuation at word[0x5e8].
  CF==1 (0x701-0x730): es=word[0x782], di=[cs:0x848]*3, cx=[cs:0x84a]*3, zero that run, word[0x780]=0x782,
        byte[0x786]=1.
Both ES bases are real-mode SEGMENTS that Ghidra lost (it used `[cs:0x848]*3` as a bare host pointer).

Store widths restored to the asm in BOTH functions -- [0x786] and [0x738] are BYTE (`c6 06 86 07 00`,
`fe 06 38 07`, `fe 0e 38 07`), [0x5e8] and [0x780] are WORD (`c7 06 e8 05 ...`).  04f1's accessors were
undefined2/undefined4 and clobbered [0x787] and [0x5ea..0x5eb]; that is corrected here too, since it is
the same two instructions in the same twin pair.
